WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.420
Hey, welcome, everybody.

00:00:01.420 --> 00:00:05.190
One of the things we're going to spend some
time talking about today are the recent protests

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:11.259
and unrest and violence and the way that people
have been trying to take advantage of that

00:00:11.259 --> 00:00:13.200
violence and unrest.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:18.270
But before we even do that, one of the things
I want to talk about is this broader context

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:24.520
in which Donald Trump is running for president
as if someone else has been president for

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:26.330
the last four years.

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:31.900
And that's just one aspect of what I want
to focus in on today.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:37.030
And that particular aspect is really unlike
anything we've seen in the modern political

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:42.650
era for presidents running for reelection,
most presidents have run for reelection very

00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:44.190
clearly on.

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:48.899
I've been in charge for four years and we're
going to get another four years.

00:00:48.899 --> 00:00:51.420
That will be similar to the last four.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:52.690
And that's good.

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:55.130
Donald Trump is doing something very, very
different.

00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:56.220
And that's what I want to talk about.

00:00:56.220 --> 00:01:00.989
Now, before we get we get into that, I guess
it's important to mention I'm leaving a lot

00:01:00.989 --> 00:01:05.750
out of this analysis in terms of things that
Donald Trump is doing.

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:08.650
Of course, this has been one of the most dishonest
presidencies.

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:12.930
The lie count is off the charts and Donald
Trump has been doing a lot of lying to justify

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:14.580
his reelection as well.

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:15.580
Okay.

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:19.820
On the issues, Donald Trump has failed to
deliver on a bunch of different campaign issues.

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:24.230
The wall replacing the health care system
on and on and on.

00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:28.290
But there's a reason that I want to focus
in on this particular aspect, because it relates

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:38.110
to the sort of gas slighty nature of the campaign,
as well as the intellectually compromised

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:44.280
element of Donald Trump's electorate, which
is that Donald Trump is framing his reelection

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:51.320
campaign as if you need to choose him instead
of what we've had for the last four years.

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:57.060
And unfortunately, it's working on a lot of
people, as evidenced by some of the interviews.

00:01:57.060 --> 00:02:02.759
When you go to these rallies that Donald Trump
has been doing, the RNC, et cetera.

00:02:02.759 --> 00:02:09.700
And the language that Trump is using suggests
somebody else has been in charge for the last

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:11.150
four years.

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:15.820
And in order to fix that, Donald Trump must
be elected.

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:20.460
When you look at this phrase, make America
great again.

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:28.680
Again, that is predicated on the implicit
understanding that Trump won in 2016.

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:32.720
And for a while he was great and he made America
great again.

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:37.980
And then that sort of fell apart, including
with coronavirus and the economy.

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:41.580
And now we need to elect Trump in order to
make America great again.

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:44.770
Again, because it's almost like Trump hasn't
been the one in charge for the last six or

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:45.770
seven months.

00:02:45.770 --> 00:02:51.490
We have to put Trump back in power to fix
problems that were actually created during

00:02:51.490 --> 00:02:55.880
Donald Trump's presidency, as if he was not
in charge during that time.

00:02:55.880 --> 00:03:01.739
This is going to be a big factor in our discussion
about protests and unrest.

00:03:01.739 --> 00:03:07.780
Donald Trump has been talking about the mass
protests and the unrest with the framing of

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:15.209
Democrat cities, as he says, run by far left
mayors, anarchists or anarchists, as he calls

00:03:15.209 --> 00:03:17.470
them, Marxists and others.

00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:22.690
The reality is that it's Trump himself who
has generated the unrest.

00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:28.260
We didn't have unrest like this when Joe Biden
was vice president for eight years.

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:30.790
And I'm going to come back to that in a little
bit.

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:35.760
There has been Donald Trump's mishandling
of so many issues.

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:41.200
But Trump is running as if other people have
been in charge for the last six months.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:45.960
And in order to get things back under control,
you need to elect Donald Trump.

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:51.990
Now, of course, any thinking person would
realize Trump is saying things are out of

00:03:51.990 --> 00:03:54.319
control with me as president.

00:03:54.319 --> 00:03:56.840
So reelect me to fix it.

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:59.590
But, of course, why would we do that?

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:02.890
Why wouldn't Trump just be able to get things
under control now?

00:04:02.890 --> 00:04:07.819
In other words, why is he saying that only
in his second term will he be able to get

00:04:07.819 --> 00:04:09.110
these things under control?

00:04:09.110 --> 00:04:12.879
And of course, when you realize that he's
been what's been generating the unrest and

00:04:12.879 --> 00:04:17.769
the discontent, the entire argument falls
apart in in some sense.

00:04:17.769 --> 00:04:23.830
Trump is almost running against himself, but
putting in Joe Biden as a proxy to take the

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:26.449
hit for Donald Trump's own failings.

00:04:26.449 --> 00:04:29.419
And I wish it weren't the case.

00:04:29.419 --> 00:04:33.379
There's really no way to say this without
offending some people.

00:04:33.379 --> 00:04:39.520
But his supporters that are eating it up are
eating it up in great part because they are

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:40.770
intellectually compromised.

00:04:40.770 --> 00:04:46.219
Now, some of them know it's B.S., but they
want Trump reelected for other reasons.

00:04:46.219 --> 00:04:47.710
And so they're just jumping on the bandwagon.

00:04:47.710 --> 00:04:50.050
But a lot of people are actually falling for
this stuff.

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:55.309
Now, there's a few different thoughts about
why Donald Trump is doing this.

00:04:55.309 --> 00:04:58.900
One thought is that this is some kind of four
dimensional.

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:03.910
Yes, he's taking credit for successes, but
painting the failings on Joe Biden or on Democratic

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:05.840
mayors or whoever the case may be.

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:13.130
And it's all kind of calculated to paint him
as the underdog despite the fact that he's

00:05:13.130 --> 00:05:14.130
the incumbent.

00:05:14.130 --> 00:05:15.130
Right.

00:05:15.130 --> 00:05:17.600
We could go into some kind of more complex
analysis.

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:23.869
The other explanation is way simpler, which
is Trump's a one trick pony.

00:05:23.869 --> 00:05:28.330
He doesn't know how to run as the incumbent.

00:05:28.330 --> 00:05:34.860
And he is running the exact same campaign
that he ran as the supposed political outsider

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:35.860
in 2016.

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:39.349
He's just running the same campaign, ignoring
the fact that he's been the president for

00:05:39.349 --> 00:05:40.710
four years.

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:43.469
We really have not seen anything like this.

00:05:43.469 --> 00:05:46.589
And it's preying upon the most ignorant voters.

00:05:46.589 --> 00:05:49.399
But that is not a guarantee that it's going
to fail to work.

00:05:49.399 --> 00:05:50.399
It very well could.

00:05:50.399 --> 00:05:51.440
It could succeed.

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:55.990
And this is why I've been sounding the alarm
now for several weeks, saying we can't write

00:05:55.990 --> 00:06:02.689
off what to many of us seem like obviously
terrible strategies as ineffective because

00:06:02.689 --> 00:06:03.689
it may work.

00:06:03.689 --> 00:06:09.349
Donald Trump genuinely expects that Americans
are going to fall for this and plenty of Americans

00:06:09.349 --> 00:06:11.030
are falling for it.

00:06:11.030 --> 00:06:17.699
Now, the other thing on top of this, which
we have to remember, is that Joe Biden was

00:06:17.699 --> 00:06:21.649
sort of in charge for eight years, in other
words, when Joe Biden was vice president.

00:06:21.649 --> 00:06:22.649
Okay.

00:06:22.649 --> 00:06:30.449
Barack Obama was the president, but we didn't
have in Obama and Biden's America chaos and

00:06:30.449 --> 00:06:36.099
unrest, the likes of which Donald Trump is
now preemptively assigning to Joe Biden.

00:06:36.099 --> 00:06:40.869
Yet you had Tea Partiers who sometimes protested.

00:06:40.869 --> 00:06:46.009
You had Ferguson, which was a very different
thing than what we have going on right now.

00:06:46.009 --> 00:06:50.599
You certainly had shootings, but that was
a gun problem, which we have not fixed.

00:06:50.599 --> 00:06:56.599
But things were actually far more calm during
the era in which Joe Biden was vice president

00:06:56.599 --> 00:06:58.610
to the president of the United States.

00:06:58.610 --> 00:07:05.199
And so at at even on the facts, you don't
even have to hypothesize what it would be

00:07:05.199 --> 00:07:07.429
like if Joe Biden were president.

00:07:07.429 --> 00:07:10.740
You can go back and see what things were like
when Joe Biden was vice president.

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:14.580
And we're going to get into later on in the
program.

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:19.729
Why is it that Trump benefits from chaos and
unrest?

00:07:19.729 --> 00:07:25.099
You would think that if people were thinking
clearly, they would say, oh, if there's chaos

00:07:25.099 --> 00:07:30.160
and unrest while Trump is president, doesn't
make sense to vote for him again, to fix it,

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:31.679
we should vote for someone else.

00:07:31.679 --> 00:07:33.119
That would be a logical assessment.

00:07:33.119 --> 00:07:37.340
I'm going to explain to you later on in the
program why why that doesn't work.

00:07:37.340 --> 00:07:42.520
Or in other words, why does Donald Trump does
benefit from the chaos and why he's trying

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:43.520
to incite it.

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:46.581
But before we go to that, let's talk about
the after effects of the Republican National

00:07:46.581 --> 00:07:46.590
Convention

